{"nodes": [{"id": "configuration_store_types_choosing_a_store", "label": "Choosing a Store", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/configuration/store-types.md", "source_location": "## Choosing a Store", "rationale": "Failover only protects callers if the last-known-good value still exists when upstream fails. A non-durable store holds it in one JVM's heap, lost on restart and invisible to other instances \u2014 so the choice is driven by deployment topology and tolerance for losing cached data.", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "configuration_store_types_inmemory", "label": "InMemory store", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/configuration/store-types.md", "source_location": "## InMemory", "rationale": "Size-capped by default (max-entries 10000, LRU eviction) so high-cardinality keys cannot grow the heap without bound. Dev/test only \u2014 a restart loses everything.", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "configuration_store_types_caffeine", "label": "Caffeine store", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/configuration/store-types.md", "source_location": "## Caffeine", "rationale": "Handles its own eviction from ReferentialPayload.expireOn so entries expire without the cleanup scheduler. Capped at max-size 10000 (Window TinyLFU). The module deliberately does not bundle Caffeine \u2014 the version is managed by spring-boot-dependencies.", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "configuration_store_types_jdbc", "label": "JDBC store", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/configuration/store-types.md", "source_location": "## JDBC", "rationale": "The only built-in durable, shared store and the recommended production choice; it is what makes failover 'clustered' since there is no special cluster mode, just shared durable state. Dialect detection is automatic via DatabaseResolver. No JDBC driver is bundled so consumers pick their own.", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "configuration_store_types_custom_store", "label": "Custom FailoverStore implementation", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/configuration/store-types.md", "source_location": "## Custom", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "configuration_store_types_expire_on_index", "label": "EXPIRE_ON index requirement", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/configuration/store-types.md", "source_location": "### Create the Table", "rationale": "The hourly cleanup DELETE ... WHERE EXPIRE_ON < ? degrades to a full table scan without an index on EXPIRE_ON, so the index is mandated in the DDL (audit I-13).", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "configuration_store_types_capacity_planning", "label": "JDBC capacity planning", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/configuration/store-types.md", "source_location": "### Capacity planning", "rationale": "One upsert per successful protected call means write volume scales with success throughput x instances. Bound it with async-executor concurrency-limit, keep TTL short, run expiry cleanup, and optionally enable the failover.live.entries gauge (off by default because it costs a COUNT(*) per scrape).", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "configuration_store_types_deployment_topologies", "label": "Deployment topologies and orthogonal modes", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/configuration/store-types.md", "source_location": "## Deployment Topologies & Modes", "rationale": "Store choice, clustering, multi-tenancy and async writes are orthogonal and compose \u2014 a clustered, multi-tenant, async JDBC store is the typical production setup. Store clustering (use JDBC) is a separate concern from dashboard cluster aggregation modes.", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "configuration_store_types_choosing_a_store", "target": "configuration_store_types_jdbc", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/configuration/store-types.md", "source_location": "## Choosing a Store", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "configuration_store_types_choosing_a_store", "target": "configuration_store_types_inmemory", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/configuration/store-types.md", "source_location": "## Choosing a Store", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "configuration_store_types_choosing_a_store", "target": "configuration_store_types_caffeine", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/configuration/store-types.md", "source_location": "## Choosing a Store", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "configuration_store_types_inmemory", "target": "reference_interfaces_failoverstore", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/configuration/store-types.md", "source_location": "## Comparison", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "configuration_store_types_caffeine", "target": "reference_interfaces_failoverstore", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/configuration/store-types.md", "source_location": "## Comparison", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "configuration_store_types_jdbc", "target": "reference_interfaces_failoverstore", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/configuration/store-types.md", "source_location": "## Comparison", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "configuration_store_types_custom_store", "target": "reference_interfaces_failoverstore", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/configuration/store-types.md", "source_location": "## Custom", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "configuration_store_types_inmemory", "target": "configuration_store_types_caffeine", "relation": "semantically_similar_to", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.85, "source_file": "docs/configuration/store-types.md", "source_location": "both non-durable, per-instance, size-capped at 10000 by default", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "configuration_store_types_caffeine", "target": "concepts_how_it_works_referentialpayload", "relation": "shares_data_with", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/configuration/store-types.md", "source_location": "Caffeine handles its own eviction using expireOn from ReferentialPayload", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "configuration_store_types_expire_on_index", "target": "concepts_how_it_works_expirycleanupscheduler", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/configuration/store-types.md", "source_location": "### Create the Table", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "configuration_store_types_capacity_planning", "target": "how_to_observability_failovermeterbinder", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/configuration/store-types.md", "source_location": "### Capacity planning \u2014 failover.live.entries", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "configuration_store_types_capacity_planning", "target": "configuration_properties_reference_store_async", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/configuration/store-types.md", "source_location": "### Capacity planning \u2014 bound the write blast radius", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "configuration_store_types_deployment_topologies", "target": "configuration_properties_reference_cluster_properties", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/configuration/store-types.md", "source_location": "!!! note Store cluster vs. dashboard cluster", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "configuration_store_types_deployment_topologies", "target": "reference_interfaces_tenantresolver", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/configuration/store-types.md", "source_location": "### Multi-tenant", "weight": 1.0}], "hyperedges": []}